{"url": "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/csci/academic-programmes/research-degree-programmes/hong-kong-phd-fellowship-scheme", "final_url": "https://www.cityu.edu.hk/csci/academic-programmes/research-degree-programmes/hong-kong-phd-fellowship-scheme", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-18", "text": "Home\nAbout Us\nNews and Events\nLocal School Outreach\nAcademic Programmes\nResearch\nStudent Life & Learning\nGlobal Outreach\nJob Opportunity\nQuick Links\nHome Academic Programmes Research Degree Programmes Hong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme\nUndergraduate Programmes\nJoint Bachelor's Degree Programmes\nUndergraduate plus Master's Degree Programmes\nMaster's Programmes\nResearch Degree Programmes\nHong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme\nHong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme\nEstablished in 2009 by the Research Grants Council (RGC), the Hong Kong PhD Fellowship Scheme (HKPFS) aims at attracting the best and brightest students in the world to pursue their PhD programmes in Hong Kong\u2019s universities.\nThe Fellowship Scheme will provide a competitive annual stipend and conference and research-related travel allowance.\nAbout the Fellowship\nCost of Living and Finance\nResearch Coordinators\nWhat the Fellowship and CityUHK Offer?\nIn HKPFS 2027/28, each Fellowship recipient will receive:\nA monthly stipend of HK$28,700 (approximately US$3,680)\nA conference and research-related travel allowance of HK$14,400 (approximately US$1,840) per year for a maximum of three years\nAn additional entrance scholarship of HK$111,300 (approximately US$14,270) covering students' full-time tuition fees and university student hall accommodation expenses in their first year of studies\nAdditional financial subsidies/ awards supported by RGC may be given to eligible Fellowship recipients\nHow to apply to CityUHK?\nStep 1:\nApplicants should first submit an initial application at the RGC's Online Application System to obtain an RGC reference number (RGC\u2019s deadline: 1 December 2026 [12:00 noon GMT + 8 hours]).\nStep 2:\nApplicants are required to submit a full application, including supporting documents, to CityUHK's Online Admission System, and quote the RGC reference number (CityUHK\u2019s deadline: 1 December 2026 [23:59 GMT + 8 hours]).\nCityUHK's Entrance Requirements\nApplicants seeking admission to PhD studies at CityUHK should satisfy the following minimum entrance requirements:\nHold a higher degree by research (or equivalent qualification) from a recognised university; or\nHold a taught Master's degree (or equivalent qualification) from a recognised university; or\nHold a Bachelor's degree with first class honours (or equivalent qualification) from a recognised university.\nEnglish Proficiency Requirements\nApplicants from an institution where the medium of instruction is not English should fulfil the following minimum English requirements:\nA score of 79 (for tests taken prior to 21 January 2026) or 4.5 (for tests taken from 21 January 2026 onwards) (Internet-based Test) in the Test of English as a Foreign Language (TOEFL)*#; or\nAn overall band score of 6.5 in International English Language Testing System (IELTS)*.\n* TOEFL and IELTS scores are considered valid for two years from the test date and must be valid at the time of submission of application to CityUHK.\n#In view of the two-year transition period during which both scoring scales would be in operation, together with the University\u2019s practice of accepting testing scores obtained within two years prior to the application submission date, both scales will be operationally recognized for up to four years from now.\nUseful Information\nPlease visit the website of our School of Graduate Studies at www.cityu.edu.hk/sgs/hkphd or contact our departmental research degree coordinators.\nLast Updated: September 2026\nAbout Us\nMessage from the Dean\nVision and Mission\nFacts and Figures\nAcademic Rankings\nPeople\nAcademic Units\nAwards and Recognitions\nContact Us\nNews and Events\n